From cbab56c141b7eec178ceb6e576038d6d480b1fce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Sebastian=20Dr=C3=B6ge?= <sebastian@centricular.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 19:26:41 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] baseparse: Add API to opt-in to allowing the base class to
 output duplicated PTS

Similar fix to

  - https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer/-/merge_requests/287
  - https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer/-/merge_requests/649
  - https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer/-/merge_requests/3462
  - https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer/-/merge_requests/7229

The main difference is that this now adds new API for parser subclasses to
explicitly opt-in to this behaviour. Enabling it unconditionally (or mixing it
with the PTS interpolation API) would break audio parsers. On duplicated PTS,
downstream of the parser would likely trigger a resync instead of interpolating
PTS based on the number of actual samples.

Also update all video parsers to actually use the new API and update the
h264parse, h265parse and h266parse tests for this situation, partially taken
from the last MR by Max Romanov. These tests were working around / asserting on
the previous, broken behaviour.

Fixes https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer/-/work_items/1515

Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/gstreamer/gstreamer/-/merge_requests/12032>
